WEBVTT

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:02.810
Thank you for breakfast!

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.670
I'll put the dishes here, okay?

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:07.800
Emi?

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:15.440
So that's why you're in a hurry, huh?

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.110
Man, what should I do?

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:18.020
What's wrong?

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:22.020
I'm not sure which one 
I should put in my deck.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:25.520
They're all cute, so I can't decide!

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.450
Morning!

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:28.780
Good morning, Aichi.

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:29.820
Morning!

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:48.620
Thank you for the food.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:51.850
The national tournament finals 
are almost here, huh?

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:53.570
Good luck!

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:55.570
Thanks.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:58.040
Aren't you hungry?

00:00:58.040 --> 00:00:58.900
Nope.

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:00.090
Thank you.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.730
I'm sorry you went to the 
trouble of making it for me...

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:07.240
I'll set it aside, so just 
eat when you're hungry, okay?

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.200
Thanks.

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:15.000
Mom, do you think Aichi's all right?

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.580
Well, he's been acting strange these days...

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.940
Knowing him, he'll be fine.

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:01.170
Emi, I'm here!

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:02.690
It's Mai!

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:06.410
I'll see you later!

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.380
See you later!

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:14.190
Golden Glow

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.400
Remember, Aichi!

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:25.060
Remember the fight you really wanted to have!

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:31.790
If Kai hadn't opened my eyes, I'd be...

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:41.490
And it wasn't just the 
people I fought against.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:45.980
I was awful to everyone in Q4, too.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:49.490
What should I do?

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:34.680
Slow down or you could 
hurt yourself. Be careful.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:36.850
Okay! See you later!

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:44.940
I understood the moment I touched the deck...

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:47.450
My true feelings!

00:04:57.270 --> 00:05:02.520
Vanguard taught me... to face things head-on.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:08.890
I learned because Kamui, 
Misaki and Kai were there.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.820
I want to keep playing Vanguard, too...

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:15.210
...with everyone in Q4!

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:18.390
I don't know if they'll forgive me...

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:23.630
...but I'll apologize to everyone 
and tell them how I feel now!

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:24.210
Card Capital

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:38.850
I-I have to tell them how I feel!

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:40.470
U-Um...

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:56.310
It's even livelier than last time, isn't it?

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.920
Card Capital Shop Tournament

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:00.900
Shop tournament?

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:03.350
That's right, Brother!

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:05.140
Isn't that why you came?

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:06.630
N-No...

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:10.280
Even though the finals of the national 
tournament haven't been held yet,

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:12.190
you're already holding the 
qualifier for the next one?

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:15.970
No, this has nothing to do 
with the national tournament.

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:21.200
This tournament is just for everyone 
who comes to Card Capital to have fun.

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:24.890
The most important thing today, 
more than winning or losing,

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:26.890
is to have a good time playing together.

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:30.100
Come on. You too, Aichi.

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:31.900
But I...

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:36.160
Oh, you don't need to 
worry about arriving late.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:37.670
No, that's not what I...

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:39.170
You can take part.

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:41.080
Let's go, Brother!

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:42.740
Here.

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:44.420
Right.

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:46.250
I'll take that!

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:50.490
I was 0.1 seconds faster than you.

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:51.870
Mr. Kishida?

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:55.500
Sure. I'll take that.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:59.820
Sendou, the last time we submitted 
our applications together,

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:02.020
you made me taste the bitterness of defeat.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:04.250
But this time, I'm going to win.

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:09.270
He just doesn't get it...

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:12.090
There is no limit to the 
number of players today.

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:14.660
Today's rule.

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:18.090
"It doesn't matter how many fights you have.

00:07:18.090 --> 00:07:21.560
The victor will be the one 
who has the most wins."

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:23.920
Oh, really?

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:25.260
That's how it is!

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:26.000
Here.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.000
Um...

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:29.190
Just hurry up!

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:32.200
Yep, you've completed your entry.

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:36.700
Come on, Brother Aichi, let's 
win like crazy today, too!

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:39.760
Misaki, you go ahead and fight, too.

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:43.480
Sub-manager and I will handle 
the entries and the judging.

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:45.980
I mean... "Manager"...

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:47.420
Right?

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:54.740
Today's shop tournament is split between 
the elementary school junior division

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.150
and the middle school-and-up senior division.

00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:57.740
Huh...

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.230
So you're in the junior division, Kamui?

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:04.030
Yeah, right! No, I'm in the senior 
division with you, Brother.

00:08:04.030 --> 00:08:08.810
There isn't anyone I wanna 
fight in the junior division!

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:09.750
Oh, Emi!

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:12.810
With Pacifica's skill, I Soulcharge 
the top card of my deck.

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:11.110
Miss Emi?!

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:13.430
You didn't know?

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:13.850
I draw one card.

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:15.990
I only got here right before you did!

00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:15.990
I put Aqua at the bottom of my deck.

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:28.710
I attack Maiden of Trailing 
Rose with Mermaid Idol, Flute!

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:33.430
When there are four or more units in the 
rear-guard, Flute gains +3000 power!

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:42.310
Then... I'll intercept with Geograph Giant.

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:57.350
I attack with Top Idol, Pacifica, 
boosted by Mermaid Idol, Sedna!

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:03.220
Pacifica also gains +3000 power when there 
are four or more units in the rear-guard!

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:05.650
I guard with Watering Elf!

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:12.000
And I intercept with Hey Yo Pineapple!

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:13.200
Hey, yo!

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:15.420
Drive trigger, check!

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:19.210
Critical trigger!

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:23.410
I'm giving the power and the 
extra critical to Pacifica!

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:36.370
I lost! You're strong, Emi!

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:41.370
I studied in order to 
build a cute, strong deck!

00:09:41.690 --> 00:09:45.580
I did try putting in a 
bunch of Neo Nectar cards

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:48.170
from the fifth booster set, 
"Awakening of Twin Blades", but...

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:50.900
Junior Proof of Victory

00:09:53.670 --> 00:09:58.350
That's so cute! If you win, you get 
a pawprint stamp from the manager!

00:09:58.350 --> 00:09:59.220
Lucky!

00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:01.180
Actually, I'm the manager...

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:02.540
But you're not listening...

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:06.890
Aichi, you came!

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:08.380
Yep.

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:10.390
You're gonna play Vanguard, right?

00:10:10.390 --> 00:10:11.130
Yeah.

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:13.830
Miss Emi is here!

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:17.920
All right! The chance for a cardfight 
just between the two of us has arrived!

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:23.240
Miss Emi, please fight me!

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:26.300
Sure, I'd love to!

00:10:30.430 --> 00:10:33.240
And if I win, please marry me!

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:36.410
Sure, I'd love to!

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:42.130
Yes! Fight! Love! Marriage!

00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:42.930
Miss Emi!

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:45.390
Kamui...?

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:52.660
M-M-Miss Emi, p-p-please fight... fight me!

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:55.130
Sure, I'd love to!

00:10:56.820 --> 00:10:59.420
J-Just like I imagined!

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:01.850
Too bad!

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:04.490
That's right.

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:07.940
It seems you can't fight with us, Kamui.

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:11.960
'Cause I'm in the junior division!

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:15.520
N-Noooo!

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.790
That's right... you said you're 
in the senior division, Kamui...

00:11:20.890 --> 00:11:22.840
I'm sorry, Kamui.

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:25.620
What's wrong, Kamui the Great?

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:26.700
WW, yo?

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:29.700
Are you guys participating too?

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:31.020
Yep!

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:32.560
In the junior division.

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:33.440
What?!

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:40.080
You'll be in hot water if you fight Miss 
Emi without my permission! Got it?!

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:53.470
Finishing Hold!

00:11:57.990 --> 00:11:59.730
Senior Proof of Victory

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:02.820
Oh, they're going at it!

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:04.630
Huh? Where's Morikawa?

00:12:05.260 --> 00:12:06.450
Go!

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:07.430
Go!

00:12:08.130 --> 00:12:10.070
Looks like Emi's having a good time...

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:16.440
Huh? Where? I hear his voice, but...

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:19.750
No one knows where I am!

00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:28.970
Whoa! I had no idea! Right, Izaki?

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:33.210
Now it's time for a fair fight.

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:41.720
No!! I forgot my strongest deck!

00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:43.380
Oh, no...

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:44.730
What did you come here for?!

00:12:45.150 --> 00:12:48.730
Of all days to forget, the shop 
tournament... Oh, the despair...

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:52.500
Can't come to a battlefield 
without your sword, right?

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:55.000
I guess that's just Lose-umi 
being Lose-umi...

00:12:55.760 --> 00:12:58.360
This is the gravest blunder of my life.

00:12:58.360 --> 00:12:59.690
Thus...

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:04.890
Please use this deck, Morikawa.

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:07.580
I-I'm not Morikawa!

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:09.810
I cannot accept another's charity.

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:12.360
Even when a samurai hasn't eaten, 
he uses an icepick like a lord.

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:14.800
That's "toothpick"! And you're a <i>ninja</i>.

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:18.390
Oh, don't be like that, Master M the Second.

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:21.110
F-Fine. If you insist, then I have no choice.

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:24.770
A constructed deck, Golden Mechanical Soldier.

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:28.060
They're all grades 1 and 2...

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:30.250
This deck seems weak...

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:33.170
Oh, well, you never know unless you try.

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:37.540
I'll have my number one disciple, 
Morikawa, try this deck out.

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:42.260
Morikawa! Morikawa! Where 
are you-degozaru, Morikawa?

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:45.070
I respect him, in a sense.

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:51.020
Sorry I took so long, Izaki!

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:52.100
All right!

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:54.250
Come, Ninja Master M!

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:55.110
Mm!

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:57.940
No, no, no! I'm Katsumi Morikawa!

00:13:57.940 --> 00:14:00.780
Just so you know, I'm borrowing today's deck.

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:04.680
In other words, it won't 
reflect my true ability.

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:06.650
But with that in mind, let's fight!

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:11.940
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:14:13.340 --> 00:14:14.570
That's a scary face!

00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:16.890
I ride Tough Boy!

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:19.150
I ride King of Sword!

00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:22.710
I ride Gold Rutile!

00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:28.390
I don't believe it! Lose-umi is 
smoothly riding one after the other!

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:36.910
I attack Deathrex with Gold Rutile!

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:41.970
I lost!

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:46.470
Wanna go one more time?

00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:47.790
Y-You bet!

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:50.390
There must be some mistake!

00:14:51.170 --> 00:14:56.560
Gold glitters for eternity. And my 
glory glitters for eternity too!

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:59.680
Tinkling, twinkling Gold Rutile!

00:15:00.010 --> 00:15:01.630
Gong!!

00:15:02.260 --> 00:15:03.500
I don't believe it...

00:15:04.430 --> 00:15:06.090
Senior Proof of Victory

00:15:06.930 --> 00:15:08.000
Excuse me...

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:09.390
Me?

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:12.200
Yeah! I'd like you to look at my deck,

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:14.660
since you're in the national 
tournament, Mr. Sendou!

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:18.150
Well, if you feel that I'm good enough...

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:19.510
Yes!!

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:23.310
You've got a Royal Paladin deck, same as me.

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:30.370
Um, instead of Alfred, should I put in one 
of my new cards, Fang of Light, Garmall?

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:34.260
If you like Alfred, I 
think he's a good choice.

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:37.320
Good! I do like Alfred!

00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:42.560
All right!

00:15:42.950 --> 00:15:45.240
I attack with Valkyrie, Laurel!

00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:47.540
Junior Proof of Victory

00:15:47.570 --> 00:15:49.540
Yay!!

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:51.560
Everyone is laughing...

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:54.540
Oh, yeah. That's right.

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:58.100
Vanguard is <i>fun</i>.

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:04.980
I was so focused on winning that 
I forgot to have a good time.

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:08.290
That really is a scary face!

00:16:09.980 --> 00:16:13.560
Gold Rutile's strongest attack!

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:15.230
Senior Proof of Victory

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:22.620
Wow! He even beat Miwa! What 
happened to Morikawa?!

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:26.120
Whoa, that Morikawa doesn't 
cut a guy any slack!

00:16:26.120 --> 00:16:31.160
And he keeps drawing the one Gold 
Rutile that's in the deck...

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:33.550
I see. It <i>is</i> a Golden 
Mechanical Soldier deck, right?

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:34.850
But this is incredible...

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:38.050
Consecutive victories!

00:16:38.050 --> 00:16:40.350
There isn't anyone who's a match for me!

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:42.630
So who'll be my next opponent?

00:16:45.010 --> 00:16:46.580
You, Aichi!

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:54.050
What's wrong?

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:54.760
O-Okay.

00:16:56.020 --> 00:16:56.900
Come on!

00:16:57.410 --> 00:16:58.200
Sure.

00:17:00.110 --> 00:17:01.990
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:10.320
I stand and draw.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:15.490
Nuts! Only one grade 3!

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:18.180
This deck is weak sauce!

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:21.020
Hey, you're saying that out loud!

00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:25.090
Anyway, I ride Gold Rutile!

00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:34.020
Trading Card Game

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:29.670
No choice. Guess I'll use some grade 2s...

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:34.300
King of Sword, Oasis Girl, Screamin' 
and Dancin' Announcer, Shout...

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:35.070
Call!

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:40.080
This is totally weak...

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:45.190
But it's a good development for that 
Golden Mechanical Soldier constructed deck...

00:17:45.190 --> 00:17:45.810
Y-Yeah...

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:47.160
There!

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:50.590
I attack with King, boosted by Oasis Girl!

00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:55.770
With a boost from Tough Boy...

00:17:56.060 --> 00:17:57.830
...Gold Rutile attacks!

00:17:58.180 --> 00:18:00.490
I guard with Flash Shield, Iseult!

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:02.550
Perfect defense, eh?

00:18:02.550 --> 00:18:04.240
But I still have this...

00:18:04.610 --> 00:18:06.070
Drive trigger check!

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:08.580
Second check...

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:12.030
I got a heal trigger!

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:16.080
I add +5000 to the power of NGM Prototype!

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:18.820
And I heal 1 point of damage!

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:22.420
I attack with Prototype, boosted by Shout!

00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:26.670
Damage trigger check!

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:30.080
Oh, no! Stand trigger!

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:31.520
Heal trigger would've been helpful...

00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:34.270
That's the end of the strongest turn.

00:18:35.160 --> 00:18:37.040
I stand and draw.

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:39.640
Everything rides on this turn...

00:18:40.290 --> 00:18:42.920
King of Knights, Alfred's Counterblast!

00:18:45.440 --> 00:18:48.860
I superior call Knight of Silence, Gallatin!

00:18:50.890 --> 00:18:54.290
With Barcgal's skill, I superior call Flogal!

00:18:56.550 --> 00:19:00.630
I attack Prototype with 
Gallatin, boosted by Flogal!

00:19:04.970 --> 00:19:08.130
I was right, it's no good without grade 3s...

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:11.140
I attack Gold Rutile with Alfred!

00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:13.400
No guard!

00:19:13.730 --> 00:19:15.400
Drive trigger check!

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:18.610
I got a critical trigger.

00:19:19.280 --> 00:19:22.970
I add +5000 to the power of the 
Gallatin that hasn't attacked yet!

00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:26.300
And I give the extra critical to Alfred!

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:30.230
What?!

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:32.710
Damage trigger, first card...

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:34.390
Second card...

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:37.800
With a boost from Flogal... Gallatin!

00:19:40.390 --> 00:19:43.660
I guard with Shining Lady and Ring Girl, Clara!

00:19:50.880 --> 00:19:52.470
I'll show you...

00:19:52.470 --> 00:19:54.130
...my strongest final turn!

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:56.620
That's taking it too far.

00:19:56.940 --> 00:19:58.440
I call the King!

00:19:58.440 --> 00:20:01.370
Oasis Girl's strongest Counterblast!

00:20:01.370 --> 00:20:02.600
+1000 power!

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:05.920
One more time!

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:11.020
There! All of the last three cards!

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:12.070
Morikawa...

00:20:12.470 --> 00:20:16.340
I attack with King, boosted by Oasis Girl!

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:19.440
I guard with Epona and Marron!

00:20:20.310 --> 00:20:24.720
It <i>is</i> incredible that he had 
five Counterblasts in a row...

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:26.460
...but if he uses them without thinking...

00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:30.620
There! I attack with Gold 
Rutile, boosted by Tough Boy!

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:31.920
I guard with Llew!

00:20:32.730 --> 00:20:34.590
And Gallatin intercepts!

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:38.810
Drive trigger strongest check...

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:41.760
What?! Strongest second check!

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:44.560
Strongest heal trigger!

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:51.290
I add +5000 to the power of the 
King that hasn't attacked yet.

00:20:51.290 --> 00:20:53.480
And I heal 1 point of damage.

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:56.920
Then King attacks with a boost from Shout!

00:20:58.000 --> 00:20:59.500
No guard.

00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:05.730
I lose.

00:21:06.560 --> 00:21:11.310
Yes!! My strongest legend is indestructible!

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:16.010
That guy's really strong when 
he uses a balanced deck?!

00:21:16.950 --> 00:21:19.190
No way! No way!

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:20.360
It had to be a fluke!

00:21:20.360 --> 00:21:22.980
I'm the strongest! Yay!

00:21:23.730 --> 00:21:24.930
Aichi...

00:21:31.090 --> 00:21:33.720
Thank goodness! Aichi 
is back to his old self!

00:21:34.200 --> 00:21:35.510
Nice fight.

00:21:35.510 --> 00:21:38.430
Brother, fight me next!

00:21:38.430 --> 00:21:39.190
Sure!

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:41.370
Well, it looks like things are okay now.

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:45.770
Sub-manager...

00:21:45.770 --> 00:21:47.100
I'm sorry!

00:21:47.470 --> 00:21:50.420
For being so rude to everyone...

00:21:50.420 --> 00:21:54.160
What are you talking about, 
Brother? Cut it out!

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:55.220
Hear, hear.

00:21:55.220 --> 00:21:56.080
But...

00:21:56.080 --> 00:21:57.450
Remember what I said before?

00:21:58.320 --> 00:22:02.190
The most important thing today is to 
have a good time playing together.

00:22:03.240 --> 00:22:05.520
Let's have fun, Brother!

00:22:09.580 --> 00:22:10.830
Welcome back.

00:22:13.310 --> 00:22:14.440
I'm back!

00:23:52.050 --> 00:23:53.360
I'm the strongest!

00:23:53.360 --> 00:23:54.470
Unbelievable!

00:23:54.470 --> 00:23:56.040
You're doing great, Morikawa!

00:23:56.040 --> 00:23:58.860
I did my best against you, but...

00:23:59.340 --> 00:24:01.610
You've still got a long way to go, Aichi.

00:24:01.610 --> 00:24:04.920
I mean, you can't see what the 
next card is going to be, can you?

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:06.430
But as for me...

00:24:06.410 --> 00:24:08.290
He's out of control, in more ways than one!

00:24:08.380 --> 00:24:10.430
Morikawa... Everyone...

00:24:10.600 --> 00:24:12.690
Next time: Songstress of the Sea.

00:24:12.820 --> 00:24:16.700
Making a lot of noise and having 
fun fights at Card Capital...

00:24:16.800 --> 00:24:19.520
I hope this image lasts forever.
